<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net" modified="2026-09-08T00:00:00.000Z" agent="architecture-doc" version="24.0.0" type="device">
  <diagram id="simple-flow" name="Simple View — Step by Step">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1200" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2380" pageHeight="3829" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />

        <mxCell id="title" value="External Users → Looker Dashboards — Step by Step (one action per box)" style="text;html=1;fontSize=21;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1C2733;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="18" width="1330" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="subtitle" value="Two ways in: (A) a person logs in at step 1 · (B) an external application that already holds a JWT joins at step 11. The JWT never detours to the browser mid-chain — Apigee receives it and calls GKE directly." style="text;html=1;fontSize=13;fontColor=#4A5A6A;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="60" width="1330" height="44" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ ROW 1 (steps 1-4) ============ -->
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;1. User clicks the portal link&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;browser goes to&lt;br&gt;portal.yourdomain.com" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#1C2733;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="120" width="310" height="118" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;2. Front Door&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;the Apigee external proxy endpoint, exposed by the external HTTP(S) Load Balancer — the only internet-facing surface&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0b5fa5&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GCP: Cloud LB (L7) · Apigee X (external proxy) · PSC&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E9F1F8;strokeColor=#0B5FA5;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="400" y="120" width="310" height="118" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;3. Routed to the UI screen&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;login page shows — the UI is &lt;b&gt;hosted internally in GKE&lt;/b&gt;, never exposed directly&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0b5fa5&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GCP: UI/NGINX pods on GKE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#1A7F4E;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="740" y="120" width="310" height="118" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;4. User enters userid + password&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;and presses Sign in&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#9a5b00&quot;&gt;(the only manual action)&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#1C2733;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="120" width="310" height="118" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ ROW 2 (steps 5-8) ============ -->
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;5. Submit passes the front door&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;rate-limit + threat checks, then lands on the UI app in GKE&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0b5fa5&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GCP: Apigee SpikeArrest · Threat Protection → GKE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E9F1F8;strokeColor=#0B5FA5;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="320" width="310" height="118" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;6. Handed to the INTERNAL Apigee proxy&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;from GKE the credentials pass to the internal proxy — never on the internet&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0b5fa5&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GCP: GKE → Apigee X (internal proxy)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E9F1F8;strokeColor=#0B5FA5;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="740" y="320" width="310" height="118" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;7. Internal proxy calls the ID&amp;amp;A API&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;the identity team's validation service&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0b5fa5&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GCP: ID&amp;amp;A microservice on GKE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4ECF8;strokeColor=#8E6AA8;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="400" y="320" width="310" height="118" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;8. Password checked against OSIS&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;ID&amp;amp;A compares the userid + password with the credential store" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4ECF8;strokeColor=#8E6AA8;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="320" width="310" height="118" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="osis" value="&lt;b&gt;OSIS DB&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;credential store" style="shape=cylinder3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=11;fillColor=#FFE6CC;strokeColor=#D79B00;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="110" y="510" width="150" height="95" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ ROW 3 (steps 9-12) ============ -->
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;9. ✔ Valid — ID&amp;amp;A creates the JWT&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;a signed JWT token — the user's pass for this session" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E7F5EE;strokeColor=#1A7F4E;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="680" width="310" height="118" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;10. JWT comes back to Apigee&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;via the internal proxy — it does NOT detour to the browser; Apigee carries on with the chain" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E7F5EE;strokeColor=#1A7F4E;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="400" y="680" width="310" height="118" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;11. Apigee validates the JWT&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;signature + expiry check at the gateway&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0b5fa5&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GCP: Apigee X (VerifyJWT policy)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E9F1F8;strokeColor=#0B5FA5;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="740" y="680" width="310" height="118" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;12. Apigee calls the GKE API — the ONE call per login&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;GET /session/bootstrap · Authorization: Bearer &amp;lt;JWT&amp;gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0b5fa5&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GCP: private network — PSC / Internal LB&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E9F1F8;strokeColor=#0B5FA5;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="680" width="310" height="118" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ ROW 4 (steps 13-15) ============ -->
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;13. GKE checks the JWT again + finds the tenant&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;double check (defense in depth) · then looks the partner up in the &lt;b&gt;tenant registry&lt;/b&gt; — unknown partner → refused&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0b5fa5&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GCP: Google Kubernetes Engine&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#1A7F4E;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="880" width="310" height="118" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;14. GKE builds everything in ONE go&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;dashboard list + the &quot;Home&quot; pick + a signed one-time Looker login URL — GKE calls Looker itself, via the reverse proxy (Apigee never touches Looker)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#1A7F4E;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="740" y="880" width="310" height="118" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;15. The browser opens the signed URL — that IS the Looker login&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Looker signs the user in, shows only this user's rows (row-level security)&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0b5fa5&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GCP: NGINX on GKE · Looker (containerized on GKE)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#1A7F4E;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="400" y="880" width="310" height="118" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="dw" value="&lt;b&gt;Data Warehouse&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0b5fa5&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;BigQuery (private IP)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="shape=cylinder3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=11;fillColor=#FFE6CC;strokeColor=#D79B00;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="440" y="1060" width="160" height="95" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ FINAL STEP ============ -->
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;16. Dashboard opens for the user&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;dashboard + tile list arrive; the session cookie is set on THIS response — the user just experienced: password in → dashboard out" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E7F5EE;strokeColor=#1A7F4E;strokeWidth=2.5;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="880" width="310" height="118" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ EDGES ROW 1 ============ -->
        <mxCell id="e1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#1C2733;strokeWidth=2;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s1" target="s2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2" value="routes /login" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#1C2733;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#4A5A6A;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s2" target="s3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e3" value="login page shown" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#1C2733;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#4A5A6A;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s3" target="s4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="w1" value="submit, over TLS" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#1C2733;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#4A5A6A;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s4" target="s5">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ EDGES ROW 2 ============ -->
        <mxCell id="e5" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#1C2733;strokeWidth=2;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s5" target="s6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e6" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#1C2733;strokeWidth=2;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s6" target="s7"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e7" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#1C2733;strokeWidth=2;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s7" target="s8"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e8osis" value="lookup" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#D79B00;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#9A5B00;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s8" target="osis"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="w2" value="✔ password correct" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#1A7F4E;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#1A7F4E;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s8" target="s9">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ EDGES ROW 3 ============ -->
        <mxCell id="e9" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#1A7F4E;strokeWidth=2;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s9" target="s10"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e10" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#1A7F4E;strokeWidth=2;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s10" target="s11"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e11" value="token OK" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#1C2733;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#4A5A6A;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s11" target="s12"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="w3" value="Bearer JWT, private network" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#0B5FA5;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10.5;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#0B5FA5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s12" target="s13">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ EDGES ROW 4 ============ -->
        <mxCell id="e13" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#1C2733;strokeWidth=2;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s13" target="s14"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e14" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#1C2733;strokeWidth=2;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s14" target="s15"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e15dw" value="query" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#D79B00;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#9A5B00;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s15" target="dw"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="w4" value="rendered dashboard back to the browser" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#1A7F4E;strokeWidth=2.5;dashed=1;fontSize=10.5;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1A7F4E;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s15" target="s16">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ ALTERNATE ENTRY: external application ============ -->
        <mxCell id="altApp" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;B. ALTERNATE ENTRY — External Application&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;a system (not a person) that &lt;b&gt;already holds a valid JWT&lt;/b&gt; — obtained from ID&amp;amp;A via its own machine login (steps 1–10 skipped)&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#9a5b00&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Rule: it can NOT call the GKE API (step 13) directly — GKE only accepts traffic from Apigee. It enters through the same front door; Apigee validates its JWT at step 11, then steps 12–16 run exactly the same.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0b5fa5&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GCP: same Apigee X external gateway — /api/** with Authorization: Bearer JWT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF7E8;strokeColor=#9A5B00;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;fontSize=11.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="700" y="505" width="390" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eAlt" value="calls /api/** with its JWT — joins at step 11" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#9A5B00;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;fontSize=10.5;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#9A5B00;" edge="1" parent="1" source="altApp" target="s11">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ NOTES ============ -->
        <mxCell id="noteAfter" value="&lt;b&gt;After the first open — nothing calls the API again:&lt;/b&gt; filters and drill-downs happen inside the dashboard; &lt;b&gt;switching dashboards&lt;/b&gt; just points the frame at another one — the live Looker session plus per-tenant folder walls decide what may open, and row-level security filters every query. Steps 1–16 (and the single API call at step 12) run again only at the &lt;b&gt;next login&lt;/b&gt;, when the hour-long session expires. &lt;b&gt;External applications (path B)&lt;/b&gt; enter at step 11 for each of their own calls." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FDF6E6;strokeColor=#D8B56A;fontSize=12;align=left;spacing=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="1230" width="1330" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="keys" value="&lt;b&gt;3 things to remember&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;🚪 &lt;b&gt;One front door:&lt;/b&gt; only step 2 (the Apigee external proxy behind the external HTTPS LB) faces the internet — the UI in GKE, the internal proxy, ID&amp;A, OSIS, the GKE API, Looker and the databases are all private.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;🎟️ &lt;b&gt;One token, checked twice, no detour:&lt;/b&gt; the password is used once (steps 4–8) to get a JWT; the JWT returns to Apigee (step 10) which validates it (step 11) and calls GKE with it as Bearer (step 12) — GKE validates it AGAIN (step 13) before Looker is touched.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;🔒 &lt;b&gt;Own data only:&lt;/b&gt; the token names the user's tenant, and Looker filters every query so each user sees only their rows (step 15, row-level security)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E3EEF7;strokeColor=#0B5FA5;fontSize=12.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="1370" width="1330" height="170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="registry" value="&lt;b&gt;Tenant Registry&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0b5fa5&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;BigQuery&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;partner → tenant" style="shape=cylinder3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=10;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1120" y="1060" width="180" height="100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eReg" value="who does this partner belong to?" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#9A5B00;strokeWidth=1.5;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#9A5B00;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s13" target="registry">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyTitle" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:17px&quot;&gt;The 16-step flow — extended (13–16 in full detail)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;tally column — text identical to the runbook Flow section" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#1C2733;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="60" width="880" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyLede" value="Steps 1–12 as agreed, then the part this runbook implements — 13 to 16 — broken down far enough that anyone can trace a click to a row of data and back." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;spacingRight=10;fillColor=#f2f4f6;strokeColor=#c9d2da;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="118" width="880" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyH0" value="&lt;b&gt;Step 1 · the click and the front door&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fillColor=#0b5fa5;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="180" width="880" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyB0" value="&lt;b&gt;1a&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;User clicks the portal link&lt;/b&gt; (bookmark, email, or partner site). DNS resolves portal.yourdomain.com to the &lt;b&gt;Global External HTTPS Load Balancer&lt;/b&gt;'s anycast IP; the browser starts the TLS handshake against the LB's Google-managed certificate.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;1b&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Why this LB exists at all:&lt;/b&gt; it is required &lt;b&gt;Apigee X plumbing&lt;/b&gt; — the external Application LB (L7) with a &lt;b&gt;PSC Network Endpoint Group&lt;/b&gt; is how the Apigee X runtime is exposed on a custom hostname. (An L4 passthrough LB was evaluated and rejected — Apigee X exposure requires L7 + PSC NEG, and L4 would also lose HTTP routing and managed certs.)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;1c&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;What is deliberately NOT here:&lt;/b&gt; Akamai and Cloud Armor were &lt;b&gt;removed by decision&lt;/b&gt; — there is no edge WAF and no edge rate-limiting. Consequence: &lt;b&gt;Apigee SpikeArrest (5b) is the only brute-force control&lt;/b&gt; in the whole chain — flagged risk, with Cloud Armor re-attachable later at this exact point with zero redesign." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=10;spacingBottom=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c9d2da;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="214" width="880" height="215" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyH1" value="&lt;b&gt;Step 2 · Apigee external gateway — the only internet-facing surface&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fillColor=#0b5fa5;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="443" width="880" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyB1" value="&lt;b&gt;2a&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;The LB forwards through the PSC NEG to the Apigee external gateway proxy.&lt;/b&gt; Nothing else in the estate accepts internet traffic: not the UI app, not the internal proxy, not the GKE API, not Looker. Every request — human or machine — enters here.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;2b&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Route match decides the lane:&lt;/b&gt; GET /login and GET /static/** → the login-UI lane (no JWT required, step 3). /auth/login → the credential lane (step 5). /api/** → the JWT-protected data lane (step 11). Unknown paths → clean 404 at the gateway; nothing leaks southbound." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=10;spacingBottom=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c9d2da;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="477" width="880" height="125" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyH2" value="&lt;b&gt;Step 3 · login page served from inside GKE&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fillColor=#0b5fa5;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="616" width="880" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyB2" value="&lt;b&gt;3a&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Apigee proxies the /login request to the UI App hosted internally in GKE.&lt;/b&gt; The UI App is a private pod behind the internal gateway — it has no public IP and no internet route; only the Apigee path reaches it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;3b&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;The login page (HTML/JS/CSS) returns to the browser&lt;/b&gt; through the same chain. One app, two duties: it &lt;i&gt;serves&lt;/i&gt; the login page now and will &lt;i&gt;receive&lt;/i&gt; the submit next — there is no separate static bucket/CDN in this design." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=10;spacingBottom=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c9d2da;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="650" width="880" height="125" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyH3" value="&lt;b&gt;Step 4 · the only manual action in the entire flow&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fillColor=#0b5fa5;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="789" width="880" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyB3" value="&lt;b&gt;4a&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;User types userid + password and presses Sign in.&lt;/b&gt; This is the single thing a human ever enters. Everything after — tenant, dashboards, identity, permissions — is derived server-side; the user never supplies or sees any of it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;4b&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;The submit leaves the browser as POST /auth/login over TLS&lt;/b&gt; to the same portal hostname — back through the LB into the Apigee external proxy. Credentials exist in transit only; the browser stores nothing." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=10;spacingBottom=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c9d2da;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="823" width="880" height="125" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyH4" value="&lt;b&gt;Step 5 · front-door checks, then hand-off to the UI app&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fillColor=#0b5fa5;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="962" width="880" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyB4" value="&lt;b&gt;5a&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;The external proxy inspects the submit BEFORE credentials travel further:&lt;/b&gt; per-IP &lt;b&gt;SpikeArrest&lt;/b&gt; (the brute-force control — see 1c), &lt;b&gt;JSONThreatProtection&lt;/b&gt; (malformed/oversized payloads), and input validation (shape of userid/password fields).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;5b&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Failures die at the gate&lt;/b&gt; with clean faults — the request never reaches identity systems. Passes → &lt;b&gt;the submit is forwarded to the UI App in GKE&lt;/b&gt;, which owns the next hop." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=10;spacingBottom=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c9d2da;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="996" width="880" height="110" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyH5" value="&lt;b&gt;Step 6 · UI app → Apigee INTERNAL proxy&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fillColor=#0b5fa5;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="1120" width="880" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyB5" value="&lt;b&gt;6a&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;From inside GKE, the UI App passes the credentials to the Apigee INTERNAL proxy.&lt;/b&gt; This proxy has no external hostname and no PSC exposure to the internet — &lt;b&gt;the browser can never reach it directly&lt;/b&gt;, which is the point: the credential path from here on runs entirely on private networking.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;6b&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Why the chain goes back through Apigee at all:&lt;/b&gt; the internal proxy is the policy point for the identity leg — consistent fault mapping, logging, and one governed door in front of ID&amp;amp;A instead of ad-hoc service-to-service calls." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=10;spacingBottom=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c9d2da;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="1154" width="880" height="140" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyH6" value="&lt;b&gt;Step 7 · internal proxy → ID&amp;amp;A API&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fillColor=#0b5fa5;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="1308" width="880" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyB6" value="&lt;b&gt;7a&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;The internal proxy calls the ID&amp;amp;A API&lt;/b&gt; (the identity team's service) with the credentials. Contract per Part 0.3: ID&amp;amp;A owns authentication only — it knows &lt;i&gt;who&lt;/i&gt; the partner is, not &lt;i&gt;which tenant&lt;/i&gt; they belong to." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=10;spacingBottom=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c9d2da;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="1342" width="880" height="65" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyH7" value="&lt;b&gt;Step 8 · ID&amp;amp;A validates against OSIS&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fillColor=#0b5fa5;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="1421" width="880" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyB7" value="&lt;b&gt;8a&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;ID&amp;amp;A checks userid + password against the OSIS database&lt;/b&gt; — the credential store, and &lt;i&gt;only&lt;/i&gt; a credential store: no tenant mapping lives there (that's the tenancy registry's job, step 13b).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;8b&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;On failure&lt;/b&gt;, the result maps to clean faults on the way back — 401 bad credentials, 423 account locked, 503 auth service down — and the browser returns to the login form. Repeated failures are throttled by SpikeArrest (5a), not by an edge WAF (there is none, 1c)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=10;spacingBottom=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c9d2da;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="1455" width="880" height="125" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyH8" value="&lt;b&gt;Steps 9–10 · JWT minted — and it never detours to the browser&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fillColor=#0b5fa5;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="1594" width="880" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyB8" value="&lt;b&gt;9a&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;✔ Valid → ID&amp;amp;A creates the signed JWT:&lt;/b&gt; claims are sub (the partner ID — the only identity field this design needs), roles, optional names, plus standard exp/iss/aud. &lt;b&gt;No tenant_id claim&lt;/b&gt; — the Data API resolves that from its own registry at step 13b.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;10a&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;The JWT travels back up the same private chain to Apigee — with NO browser detour.&lt;/b&gt; Apigee holds the token and continues the flow server-side toward the first dashboard render; the browser is still waiting on its login submit. (The HttpOnly cookie is set only at step 16a, on the dashboard response — not here.)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=10;spacingBottom=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c9d2da;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="1628" width="880" height="140" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyH9" value="&lt;b&gt;Step 11 · Apigee VerifyJWT — the gate every /api/** request passes forever&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fillColor=#0b5fa5;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="1782" width="880" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyB9" value="&lt;b&gt;11a&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Apigee's VerifyJWT policy validates the token&lt;/b&gt;: signature against ID&amp;amp;A's &lt;b&gt;JWKS URI&lt;/b&gt; (public keys, so no shared secret), plus exp, iss, aud. Invalid/expired → 401 → the browser lands back on /login.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;11b&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;This gate is permanent:&lt;/b&gt; the session-bootstrap call at each login and every ALT external-application call enter at exactly this step with a token. (Human dashboard clicks after login never come back here — they ride the live Looker session, 16b.) Login (1–10) is just the way humans obtain a token." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=10;spacingBottom=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c9d2da;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="1816" width="880" height="125" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyH10" value="&lt;b&gt;Step 12 · Apigee → GKE Data API — exactly ONE call per login&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fillColor=#0b5fa5;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="1955" width="880" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyB10" value="&lt;b&gt;12a&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Apigee strips ALL client-supplied identity headers&lt;/b&gt; (nothing the browser sent survives), then injects trusted headers from the &lt;i&gt;verified&lt;/i&gt; claims — X-User-Id, X-Roles — purely informational: the API re-derives everything from the JWT itself (13a) and resolves tenant on its own (13b).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;12b&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;The call goes out as Authorization: Bearer &amp;lt;JWT&amp;gt; over PSC/mTLS&lt;/b&gt; to the internal gateway fronting the Data API. The NetworkPolicy (B.21) makes this the &lt;i&gt;only&lt;/i&gt; admissible path — no other pod, VPC peer, or internet source can reach the API. In the single-call pattern this request is GET /api/v1/session/bootstrap — the only Apigee→API call of the entire session. Hand-off complete: steps 13–16 below are what this runbook builds." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=10;spacingBottom=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c9d2da;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="1989" width="880" height="155" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyH11" value="&lt;b&gt;Step 13 · the API re-establishes trust — in code, not config&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fillColor=#1A7F4E;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="2158" width="880" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyB11" value="&lt;b&gt;13a&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;JWT re-validated inside the pod&lt;/b&gt; (app/auth.py): signature fetched-and-cached from the JWKS URL, exp/iss/aud/sub required, roles claim must exist. Defense in depth — even if something ever bypassed Apigee, the pod refuses on its own.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;13b&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Tenant resolved from the tenancy registry&lt;/b&gt; (app/registry.py): get_tenant(sub) — one internal SELECT on the BigQuery tenant_registry dataset joining partner_users → tenants, cached 60 s per partner; with the single-call pattern this runs once per login, so BigQuery’s lookup latency never touches a click. &lt;b&gt;Not&lt;/b&gt; an extra network hop in the flow; the JWT carries no tenant claim (OSIS doesn't know tenants — the registry is the authority).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;13c&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Fail closed:&lt;/b&gt; unknown partner, disabled partner, or suspended tenant → 403 partner not provisioned. Never a default tenant — an error is the safe failure. (Flipping a registry status is your ≤60 s kill switch.)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=10;spacingBottom=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c9d2da;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="2192" width="880" height="215" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyH12" value="&lt;b&gt;Step 14 · from claims to a one-time Looker key&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fillColor=#1A7F4E;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="2421" width="880" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyB12" value="&lt;b&gt;14a&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Dashboard resolved&lt;/b&gt; (app/looker.py): the tenant's Looker folder Partners/{tenant} is listed via the SDK (5-min cache). First render (no click yet) → the dashboard titled &lt;b&gt;&quot;Home&quot;&lt;/b&gt;, else the first in the folder. The allow-list governs this bootstrap selection; after bootstrap, dashboard switching is authorized by Looker folder ACLs (F.8/F.9) — see 16b.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;14b&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Capability chosen&lt;/b&gt;: roles[0] from the JWT → hardcoded ROLE_MAP → permissions + models. Unknown role → 403.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;14c&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;The signed SSO embed URL is minted&lt;/b&gt; — sdk.create_sso_embed_url(...) with: external_user_id = &quot;{tenant}::{sub}&quot; (the identity Looker will allocate its own user for), external_group_id = tenant, user_attributes = {&quot;tenant_id&quot;: tenant} (the RLS key), permissions/models, session_length=3600, force_logout_login=True. This call goes &lt;b&gt;from the GKE API through the reverse proxy to Looker&lt;/b&gt; — Apigee is never involved with Looker in any direction. Looker signs the payload server-side with the &lt;b&gt;embed secret&lt;/b&gt; and returns a URL valid for seconds, single-use (nonce). &lt;b&gt;This is the programmatic twin of the embed URL a Looker admin can generate by hand in the Looker UI&lt;/b&gt; (a dashboard’s Embed / SSO-URL generator, or the docs’ sso-url tool) — same mechanism, but here it is minted &lt;b&gt;automatically, per user, per login, at exactly this stage&lt;/b&gt;: inside the bootstrap, wire call POST /api/4.0/embed/sso_url (B.16b), before the bootstrap response is assembled. Nobody ever generates one manually in production.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;14d&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Returned upstream — the bootstrap payload&lt;/b&gt;: {tenant, dashboards[], home_dashboard_id, embed_url, navigation{embed_base, embed_domain, session_length}} → Apigee → browser. One response carries everything the portal will need for the whole session; the signed URL is never logged or cached anywhere." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=10;spacingBottom=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c9d2da;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="2455" width="880" height="365" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyH13" value="&lt;b&gt;Step 15 · opening the URL IS the Looker login&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fillColor=#1A7F4E;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="2834" width="880" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyB13" value="&lt;b&gt;15a&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;The SPA sets the URL as the iframe src.&lt;/b&gt; The browser loads it against the public embed host → reverse proxy → Looker.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;15b&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Looker verifies&lt;/b&gt; the HMAC signature with the same embed secret, checks time/nonce (replay), and checks the parent origin against the &lt;b&gt;Embedded Domain Allowlist&lt;/b&gt; (D.5). Any mismatch → refused frame.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;15c&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Identity allocation&lt;/b&gt;: Looker looks up external_user_id. First ever visit → it &lt;b&gt;auto-creates an embed user&lt;/b&gt; (its own internal user_id, keyed to yours forever). Returning visit → same user matched, and groups/permissions/attributes are &lt;b&gt;re-stamped from this login's payload&lt;/b&gt; (grant changes apply on next login). Auto-added to &lt;b&gt;&quot;Embed Group {tenant}&quot;&lt;/b&gt; → which folder ACLs (F.8) recognize.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;15d&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Session opens in the iframe&lt;/b&gt; — Looker sets its session cookie (SameSite=None; Secure, E.1) and renders the requested dashboard shell.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;15e&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Every tile queries through RLS&lt;/b&gt;: tiles stream over WebSockets (E.3); for each query, the LookML access_filter binds orders.tenant_id to the user attribute — Looker itself appends WHERE orders.tenant_id = 'acme'. The user cannot see, remove, or bypass it; it applies to drill-downs, downloads and merges too.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;15f&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Data comes back private&lt;/b&gt;: the Looker connection runs as the single looker-bq-sa service account (jobUser@project + dataViewer@dataset only, F.2) against BigQuery / Cloud SQL over private IP. Only tenant-filtered rows flow up into the tiles." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=10;spacingBottom=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c9d2da;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="2868" width="880" height="380" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyH14" value="&lt;b&gt;Step 16 · the response, the cookie, and every request after&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fillColor=#1A7F4E;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="3262" width="880" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyB14" value="&lt;b&gt;16a&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;The dashboard travels back&lt;/b&gt;: Looker → reverse proxy → (iframe content directly to the browser); the portal page around it came back through GKE API → Apigee → LB. On &lt;b&gt;this&lt;/b&gt; response the portal's &lt;b&gt;HttpOnly session cookie&lt;/b&gt; (carrying the JWT) is set — not earlier.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;16b&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Every dashboard switch after this is an iframe navigation — no Apigee, no GKE API, no new signed URL.&lt;/b&gt; The SPA sets iframe.src = navigation.embed_base + id + &quot;?embed_domain=…&quot; (values from the bootstrap payload). The browser already holds the Looker embed-session cookie (15d): Looker authenticates the navigation from the session, &lt;b&gt;authorizes it via folder ACLs&lt;/b&gt; (the user's embed group can open only Partners/{tenant}, F.8/F.9), and RLS applies to every tile query exactly as in 15e. A hand-crafted id from another tenant's folder → Looker refuses the page.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;16c&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;What still reaches the API after login: nothing.&lt;/b&gt; One bootstrap per login is the entire Apigee→GKE budget. ALT external applications are the exception by nature — each of their calls enters at step 11 with their own token. Registry suspension (13c) blocks a partner's &lt;i&gt;next login&lt;/i&gt; within ≤60 s; it does not kill a &lt;i&gt;live&lt;/i&gt; embed session — for an immediate hard kill, disable the embed user in Looker admin (the session dies on its next request).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;16d&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;b&gt;Expiry — aligned by design:&lt;/b&gt; session_length=3600 matches the JWT lifetime: one login buys one working hour. When the Looker session lapses, the iframe bounces to a login redirect; the SPA detects it (or the timer from navigation.session_length fires) and returns the user to /login — a fresh login repeats steps 1–16 and issues exactly one new bootstrap. Grant changes (new dashboards, role changes) therefore take effect at next login, not mid-session — an accepted trade of the single-call pattern." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=10;spacingBottom=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c9d2da;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="3296" width="880" height="365" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tallyAlt" value="&lt;b&gt;ALT — external application:&lt;/b&gt; a system already holding a valid JWT (machine login with ID&amp;amp;A) calls /api/** through the &lt;b&gt;same front door&lt;/b&gt; and joins at step 11; steps 1–10 are skipped. It can &lt;b&gt;never&lt;/b&gt; call the GKE API directly — the NetworkPolicy admits only the Apigee path — and it passes the same registry + allow-list + RLS chain as a human. Machine partners need a partner_users row like anyone else." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=10;fillColor=#E7F5EE;strokeColor=#1A7F4E;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1440" y="3675" width="880" height="80" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
